# 05 · Security

## Security Posture
Apply secure-by-default practices at every trust boundary.

## Secrets and Credentials
- Never commit secrets or private keys to source control.
- Use environment/secret managers and rotation policies.
- Minimize secret exposure in logs, telemetry, and client binaries.

## Authentication and Authorization
- Enforce least privilege.
- Validate identity and authorization for every protected action.
- Expire/revoke tokens and sessions safely.

## Input and Data Handling
- Treat all external input as untrusted.
- Validate and sanitize input at boundaries.
- Use parameterized queries and safe encoding/output escaping.

## Dependency and Supply Chain
- Keep dependencies updated and supported.
- Scan dependencies and containers/artifacts for known vulnerabilities.
- Pin and verify critical build inputs where appropriate.

## Operational Security
- Ensure audit-ready logs for sensitive actions.
- Rate-limit abuse-prone endpoints/actions.
- Define incident response steps and escalation ownership.
